    "funding": "DFG projects KL 1873/1-1 and SE 1789/1-1",
    "papers": [
      {
        "label": "Seyfried, Rupprecht, Passon, Steffen, Klingsch, Boltes: New insights into pedestrian flow through bottlenecks. Transportation Science 43 (2009) 395-406",
        "url": "https://doi.org/10.1287/trsc.1090.0263"
      },
      {
        "label": "Seyfried et al.: Enhanced empirical data for the fundamental diagram and the flow through bottlenecks. PED 2008 (Springer 2010)",
        "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/0810.1945"
      },
      {
        "label": "Liddle et al.: An experimental study of pedestrian congestions: influence of bottleneck width and length (arXiv 2009)",
        "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/0911.4350"
      }
    ],
    "method": "PedPy compute_n_t on a measurement line; flow = (k1 - k0) / (t_k1 - t_k0) over the crossings ranked k0..k1 (1 / mean time gap); specific flow = flow / b. Same code (sim/bottleneck_flow.py) for the experiment and the simulation.",
    "measurement_line": "bottleneck entrance, y = 0, from x = -b/2 to x = b/2",
    "steady_window": "crossings 10 to 150: skips the first 9 people (start-up) and ends at the 150th person like Liddle et al. (2009)",
    "engine": "JuPedSim 1.4.2 via the Showtime sim image (Tier 3)",
    "model": "collision-free speed model (app default), with the app's squeeze and unstick rules active",
    "pedpy_version": "1.5.1",
    "sim_image": "showtime-sim:validation",
    "agent_radius_m": 0.22,
    "walk_speed": "normal(1.34, 0.26) m/s clipped to 0.6-2.0; 5% slow walkers at 0.7 m/s",
    "sim_dt_s": 0.025,
    "frame_hz": 4.0,
    "seeds": [
      1,
      2,
      3
    ],
    "app_defaults": true,
    "generated_at": "2026-10-14T23:22:55+00:00",
    "assumptions": [
      "Geometry from the archive metadata (wkt_geometry and parameters): corridor 7 m wide in front of the bottleneck, bottleneck b x l, walls 5 cm thick; coordinates in the archive's frame (entrance on y = 0).",
      "The holding area is not specified in the metadata or papers: it spans the corridor width and ends 4 m before the entrance ('bottleneck_distance'); its depth gives an initial density of 3.3 persons/m2 (the value of the group's 2005 series, Seyfried et al. 2009), e.g. 7.36 m for 170 people.",
      "Behind the bottleneck: an open area 8 m wide and 1 m deep (the metadata's bounding box), whose far edge is the exit, so the exit never limits the flow.",
      "Everyone starts walking at t = 0 (no reaction-time spread); the participants were soldiers told to walk normally, the simulation uses the app's adult walking speeds.",
      "Real trajectories are head positions at 25 fps; simulated positions are body centres at 4 fps (app default output rate)."
    ],
    "experimental_repeat": "Run l4 repeats the b120 setup (b = 1.2 m, l = 4 m, 178 people): 2.36 /s measured with the same method"
  },
